y (Jackson): about 9,000 regular ballots still expected, where Colom leads the counted vote by 61 points. If Hinds turns out to be nearly finished, Colom's chance falls to about 82%.", "Rankin County: about 6,000 still expected, where Hyde-Smith leads by 26 points. It is the biggest offset to Hinds.", "Affidavit (provisional) ballots: 0 of 82 counties have reported official counts so far; the rest are estimated.", "Voters who cast an affidavit ballot for lack of photo ID have five business days (to about Nov. 10) to show ID at the circuit clerk's office. Mail ballots postmarked by Nov. 3 count if they arrive by then too.", "Mississippi has no automatic recount and no runoff in this race. A recount needs a court order."], "changed": {"since": "1 PM", "head": "Colom's chance held at 97%; most likely final margin Colom +10,100.", "items": ["No new votes were counted.", "AP changed its estimate of ballots left to count in 1 county (47,050 to 46,750 statewide). Biggest effects: Yazoo, 300 fewer (Colom +19 pts there). Together these shift the expected outcome about 60 votes toward Hyde-Smith.", "Hinds County has not posted new numbers yet."]}, "summary": "Colom is favored, but the race is not over. Colom leads by 1,724 votes with about 46,800 ballots left to count. The biggest batch is in Hinds County (about 9,000), where Colom is winning about 4 in 5 votes.", "page_version": "ca50ffb0"}